window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_c-aab643d98f53c617"]={"key":"ny_c-aab643d98f53c617","group":"ny_c","uid":"aab643d98f53c617","rank":11,"title":"authored doc calderbrook serial negotiating brief","occupation":"editors","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_c3","prompt":"You are Naledi Khouri, features editor at Ashcombe Media, and I need a concise negotiating brief before your call on Thursday with Agnes Hargrove of Overbrook Associates, who represents retiring lock-keeper Iris Nightingale. Iris’s river diaries are being considered for a serial extract in our October issue, but Agnes has already declined one offer and says Overbrook wants the run to appear in publication week. Our timing matters because Ashcombe Media needs the material in hand before a rival festival preview, and the 1997 flood chapter names the water company; that chapter is the part we most need to preserve. Fee, extract count, access to photographs, and jacket credit are all potentially exchangeable, but a poorly handled concession sequence could leave us with no meaningful term to trade for the flood chapter. Agnes is expected to counter at least twice. Put the negotiating position into `serial_rights_negotiating_brief.docx` and save it at the top level of the working directory, using exactly that filename. Keep it to one page and write it for me and Felix Donnelly in legal counsel, not for publication. I need one explicit reading of the timing conflict, a clear distinction between the term we must protect and terms we should seek if affordable, a proposed opening position, and a compact concession sequence that remains usable through two counters. Include the assumptions behind any proposed figures or dates and do not invent facts about the diary, the water company, Iris’s intentions, or Overbrook’s authority. Treat the brief as an internal negotiating aid: it should identify what can be said, what must be verified before publication, and what must not be presented as an established allegation or legal conclusion. Actively discourage using the flood chapter as a bluff, threat, or implied finding. End with one clear negotiating position rather than a list of unresolved next steps, and leave out a draft contract, system instructions, publicity copy, and a recommendation about whether the water company did anything wrong.\n\n---\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `serial_rights_negotiating_brief.docx` — A one-page internal negotiating brief for the Thursday serial-rights call. (Must be saved in the top level of the solver's working directory.; Must be exactly one page when rendered.; Must be usable by Naledi Khouri and Felix Donnelly without a follow-up question.; Must distinguish supported facts, assumptions, negotiable terms, and matters requiring verification.; Must not make a legal, factual, or editorial finding about the water company.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/serial_rights_negotiating_brief.docx","bytes":39725,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/57c83ba8fe01b93a1e57ddd550e8cc4ddecfa9a6c0c71794a91968cfc28e4d2e.docx","sha256":"57c83ba8fe01b93a1e57ddd550e8cc4ddecfa9a6c0c71794a91968cfc28e4d2e","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"SERIAL RIGHTS — THURSDAY CALL BRIEF\nINTERNAL • Naledi Khouri, Features Editor | Felix Donnelly, Legal Counsel | October issue\nSUPPORTED CALL CONTEXT\nThursday call with Agnes Hargrove, Overbrook Associates, representing retiring lock-keeper Iris Nightingale. One earlier offer was declined. Proposed transaction: serial extract from Iris Nightingale’s river diaries.\nTIMING READING (CHOSEN)\nTreat Overbrook’s ‘publication week’ request as a release/appearance condition, not a reason to delay delivery. Seek material before the rival festival preview under a confidentiality/embargo condition; run it in the October issue’s publication week. This preserves competitive planning value without promising publication.\nPRIORITY, GUARDRAILS & AUTHORITY\nPROTECT — NOT A TRADE\nSEEK IF AFFORDABLE — TRADABLE\nCALL AUTHORITY / STOP\nRight to include the 1997 flood chapter that names the water company. This is the indispensable editorial objective; do not reduce, defer, or barter it away.\nFee; extract count; separately licensed access to/selectable photographs; and agreed jacket credit wording/placement, subject to final design. These are distinct currencies, not automatic diary rights.\nNaledi owns the call posture. Felix confirms rights scope and any language before commitment. Walk away from a package excluding the flood chapter or preventing pre-festival access; do not promise publication, legal clearance, or factual endorsement.\nOPENING PACKAGE — INTERNAL ASSUMPTIONS, NOT MARKET FACTS\nSAY / OFFER\nCONDITIONS TO STATE\nPropose £2,000 opening fee (internal assumption), one serial extract including the 1997 flood chapter, and a proposed delivery window before the rival festival preview. Offer a standard contributor credit; no jacket placement is guaranteed. Ask whether separate photo permission is available.\nConditional on agreement of: October publication-week appearance; confidential pre-festival delivery/embargo; defined print/digital format, territory, term, exclusivity and any approval right; text/photo permissions kept separate; and Felix’s review. Proposed figures/dates require agreement.\nCONCESSION LADDER — RETAIN A LIVE TERM THROUGH TWO COUNTERS\nSTAGE\nGIVE (ONLY IF)\nGET / KEEP\nOpening\n£2,000; 1 extract; ask for photo option; contributor credit.\n1997 flood chapter + pre-festival confidential delivery; October publication-week appearance.\nCounter 1\nIf timing/access is accepted: allow 2 extracts OR pay for a defined, separately granted photo selection (not both by default).\nKeep flood chapter; secure pre-festival delivery/embargo and written scope. Hold fee and jacket credit.\nCounter 2\nIf scope and timing are confirmed: move fee only to £3,000 ceiling (internal assumption) OR offer agreed jacket-credit wording subject to final design/approval—not a guaranteed placement.\nKeep flood chapter, delivery/embargo, and separate photo permission. Do not concede a third currency without Felix’s confirmation.\nWHAT THE CALL MAY SAY / PUBLICATION BOUNDARY\nCAN SAY NOW\nVERIFY BEFORE ANY PUBLICATION\nAshcombe seeks a serial extract and values the 1997 chapter; timing and commercial terms are negotiable subject to agreement and review. Acquiring the chapter’s text rights is not permission or factual endorsement to characterize the water company’s conduct. Do not use the flood chapter as a bluff, threat, leverage by implied accusation, or finding about the water company.\nConfirm authority, text/version, rights scope, and photo ownership/permission. Fact-check names, dates, quotations and available records; secure appropriate attribution and a response opportunity where warranted. The diary, and its inclusion in a package, does not by itself establish that the water company acted wrongly.\nNEGOTIATING POSITION: Hold firm on confidential pre-festival access to a serial extract including the 1997 flood chapter, with October publication-week appearance; trade only the four commercial currencies in the stated order and subject every commitment to written agreement and Felix’s review.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief identifies the Thursday call, the October publication target, and the relevant parties or roles.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered brief opening or context area.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the call timing, October timing, and the editor, rights representative, diary author, or counsel are identifiable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief states that the requested material is a serial extract from Iris Nightingale's river diaries.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Brief scope statement.","grader_hint":"Look for a clear description of the proposed rights transaction, not merely a generic reference to publication."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief identifies the 1997 flood chapter naming the water company as the indispensable editorial objective.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Priority or objective language in the brief.","grader_hint":"The chapter must be treated as the central protected outcome rather than as just another item in a list."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief explicitly distinguishes the protected flood-chapter right from the terms that are exchangeable.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Must-have/should-have or equivalent classification.","grader_hint":"Accept either defensible terminology, provided the boundary is unambiguous and the flood chapter is not classified as merely desirable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief makes one deliberate choice about how to handle publication-week timing versus obtaining the material before the rival festival preview.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Stated interpretation and rationale.","grader_hint":"There are two reasonable readings; award credit when one is selected, explained briefly, and used consistently rather than left as an unresolved either/or."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The chosen timing position is connected to the competitive value of having the material before the rival festival preview.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timing rationale.","grader_hint":"The brief should explain why timing matters to Ashcombe Media, not merely repeat both dates."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief records that one offer has already been declined.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Negotiation history.","grader_hint":"Look for the prior declined offer as context for the opening posture."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief gives an opening position that addresses timing, the flood chapter, and at least the principal commercial terms.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Opening offer or opening position section.","grader_hint":"The opening position may use proposed figures or ranges, but it must be a coherent package rather than disconnected wishes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The concession sequence has a discernible order and does not spend the indispensable flood-chapter objective first.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Ordered concessions or negotiation ladder.","grader_hint":"Accept a table, numbered sequence, or compact prose. The sequence must preserve leverage around the protected chapter."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The concession sequence treats fee, extract count, photo access, and jacket credit as distinct tradable currencies.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Concession ladder.","grader_hint":"Each of the four terms should be separately identifiable and capable of being exchanged, limited, or withheld."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief shows what Ashcombe Media seeks in return for each material concession.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Paired give/get language.","grader_hint":"A list of concessions without reciprocal conditions does not satisfy this item."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The sequence remains usable after at least two counters from Agnes Hargrove.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Counter-one and counter-two responses or equivalent ladder.","grader_hint":"Look for at least two staged responses, each with a condition or remaining reserve, not just the phrase 'expect two counters.'"},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief identifies a walk-away boundary or unacceptable outcome concerning the protected chapter or the timing objective.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Boundary, reservation, or stop condition.","grader_hint":"The boundary may be conditional, but it must tell the caller what cannot be traded away."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any proposed fee or quantity is labeled as an assumption, ceiling, range, or opening figure rather than presented as a known market or contractual fact.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Labels adjacent to figures.","grader_hint":"Award credit when the document makes clear which numbers are internal proposals and avoids false precision."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any proposed dates or timing windows are identified as proposed or conditional and are internally consistent with the October issue and pre-festival objective.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Timing terms in the brief.","grader_hint":"Do not require a particular date; check that the proposed timing can logically occur before publication and is not asserted as supplied fact."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief states the intended publication or extract scope, including the fact that extract count is negotiable.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scope and concessions language.","grader_hint":"The document should not silently expand the assignment into a complete-book acquisition or unrelated content."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief addresses the practical rights scope that must be confirmed for a serial extract, such as term, territory, format, exclusivity, or approval rights.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rights-scope checklist or negotiation terms.","grader_hint":"Credit a concise, professionally relevant scope treatment; do not require every possible contract clause."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief separates the right to use the flood chapter from permission to describe or characterize the water company's conduct.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Editorial/legal boundary language.","grader_hint":"The document must show that acquiring text is not the same as establishing the truth of its allegations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief identifies factual verification, attribution, or source-checking needs before publication of the water-company material.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Verification or publication-condition language.","grader_hint":"Accept verification of names, dates, quotations, records, or attribution; the brief need not prescribe a legal investigation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief expressly says that the diary or its inclusion in the package does not by itself establish that the water company acted wrongly.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Limitation or non-assertion language.","grader_hint":"This must be an explicit doctrinal boundary, not merely an absence of a defamatory statement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief actively discourages using the flood chapter as a bluff, threat, or implied accusation during negotiation.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Direct caution in the brief.","grader_hint":"Look for an affirmative instruction or warning against the misuse, not only neutral wording."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief states that Ashcombe Media must not promise publication, legal clearance, or factual endorsement before the relevant review and agreement.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Reservation or authority boundary.","grader_hint":"The limitation may be expressed as a call-handling rule or a condition of any offer."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief treats photo access as a distinct permission or deliverable rather than assuming that diary rights automatically include photographs.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Photo-rights language.","grader_hint":"Credit when ownership, permission, selection, or access is recognized as needing separate agreement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief treats jacket credit as a negotiable attribution or placement term and does not imply that a credit is guaranteed without agreement.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Credit term in the concession sequence.","grader_hint":"The wording should preserve the distinction between offering credit and promising a final design or placement."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief identifies who owns the call position and when Felix Donnelly's legal input or confirmation is needed, without turning the document into legal advice.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Roles and escalation boundary.","grader_hint":"Look for concrete ownership and a sensible legal-review boundary, not a vague 'check with legal.'"},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief distinguishes what can be said in the negotiation from what must be verified before publication.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Two-column distinction, labels, or equivalent prose.","grader_hint":"The distinction should be operational enough to guide the Thursday call."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The brief does not invent details about Iris Nightingale's diary, the water company, Overbrook Associates' authority, or the prior offer.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Assertions throughout the submitted document.","grader_hint":"Check unsupported specifics and award only when invented background facts are absent or clearly labeled as assumptions."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The brief is a usable internal call aid: a reader can identify the objective, opening position, trade order, boundaries, and verification limits without asking the author to interpret it.","weight":5.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole rendered document.","grader_hint":"Judge practical usability, hierarchy, concise wording, and whether the sequence can be followed during a live call."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document ends with one clear negotiating position rather than unresolved alternatives or a list of next steps.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final paragraph or closing callout.","grader_hint":"The final statement should resolve the chosen posture while retaining appropriate factual and legal reservations."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The document does not contain a draft contract, system click-through instructions, publicity copy, or a recommendation about whether the water company did anything wrong.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Whole rendered document.","grader_hint":"This is a scope-compliance credit item: award when the excluded material is absent, without separately scoring each exclusion."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The rendered DOCX is no more than one page.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered page count.","grader_hint":"Render with a standard offline office renderer and count pages; do not infer page count from source XML alone."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The required DOCX exists at the top level of the working directory with the exact requested filename.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Filesystem and document metadata.","grader_hint":"Check exact case, extension, and location."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is an editorial rights-negotiation brief for a small media team preparing to acquire a serial extract from a personal river diary. The document must help a features editor brief internal counsel and conduct a focused call without turning an unresolved account into a factual or legal assertion.","difficulty_sources":["bounded negotiation judgment about which rights term is indispensable and which terms can be exchanged","sequencing concessions while preserving leverage through multiple expected counters","distinguishing supported editorial facts from legal, reputational, or contractual assertions","drawing a must-have versus should-have boundary in a compact brief"],"authoring_plan":{"purpose":"Construct a compact gold negotiating brief that demonstrates editorial-rights judgment while preserving doctrinal boundaries around allegations, attribution, and publication authority.","source_constraints":["There are no reference files. All factual premises available to the solver are those in the request.","Use only the named people and organizations from the request; do not add biographical, contractual, legal, or historical facts.","Any monetary amount, extract count, date, or deadline beyond the supplied October, Thursday, and pre-festival facts must be visibly labeled as an internal assumption, proposal, range, ceiling, or condition."],"required_behaviour":["Make the 1997 flood chapter naming the water company the protected objective.","Classify fee, extract count, photo access, and jacket credit as tradable terms, while making a deliberate must/should distinction.","Choose and explain one coherent reading of the publication-week versus pre-festival timing conflict.","Provide an opening package, then an ordered concession ladder with reciprocal asks and at least two counter stages.","Reserve a meaningful walk-away boundary so the indispensable objective is not casually spent.","Treat text rights, photo rights, attribution/jacket credit, and publication timing as separable permissions or terms.","State what can be said in the call and what requires verification before publication.","Explicitly state that diary material does not establish wrongdoing by the water company and discourage bluffing, threats, or implied accusations using the chapter.","Avoid promises of publication, legal clearance, or factual endorsement before agreement and review.","End on one clear negotiating position, not unresolved alternatives or a next-steps list."],"gold_derivation":"The gold should be a one-page DOCX written as an internal brief, with compact sections or a table chosen by the build agent. Populate a plausible opening package and concession ladder using clearly marked internal assumptions rather than fixed answer-key numbers. Verify the gold by walking each rubric predicate against the rendered document, especially the reciprocal give/get logic, two-counter sequence, must/should boundary, non-assertion language, active anti-bluff warning, and final position."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"supplied_template"},"reference_files":[],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"serial_rights_negotiating_brief","filename":"serial_rights_negotiating_brief.docx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document","description":"A one-page internal negotiating brief for the Thursday serial-rights call.","required":true,"constraints":["Must be saved in the top level of the solver's working directory.","Must be exactly one page when rendered.","Must be usable by Naledi Khouri and Felix Donnelly without a follow-up question.","Must distinguish supported facts, assumptions, negotiable terms, and matters requiring verification.","Must not make a legal, factual, or editorial finding about the water company."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"document_information","work_product":"news_editorial_package","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"editors","sector":"information","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":1.5,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"Have one editorial-rights practitioner draft the reference brief from the occupational constraints and one independent reviewer check that every rubric item is observable, that the timing choice is deliberate, and that the document remains doctrinal rather than making an unsupported legal or factual finding.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["No supplied source files exist, so proposed figures and dates must be framed as internal assumptions rather than compared with an external answer key.","Two timing interpretations are intentionally acceptable; grading should assess deliberate consistency and defensibility, not one mandatory choice.","The one-page limit requires compact treatment of rights scope and verification boundaries rather than exhaustive contract drafting."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"结构/材料验收记录","detail":"validated 属于结构、防泄漏、材料推进验收；没有内容正确率结论。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:41:24+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:41:24+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:41:24+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:41:24+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R21', 'R30', 'R32']","checked_at":"2026-08-25T00:41:24+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_c3/runs/aab643d98f53c617","declared_deliverables":["serial_rights_negotiating_brief.docx"]};
